<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Gubb&amp;Inggs jumps back into interim profit.</title>
<headline>Gubb&amp;Inggs jumps back into interim profit.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     15.8	  vs  352.0  loss</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  -	    vs   -</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    0.32	 vs    7.15 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    0.32	 vs    7.15 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			  -	    vs   -</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    7.38	 vs    9.88</p>
<p>    Turnover		 179.88	 vs  140.57</p>
<p>Full name: Gubb &amp; Inggs Ltd, clothing, footwear and textiles</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that the benefits of cost-cutting and efficiency improvement programmes had yet to impact on financial results. But it added it was confident these steps, together with rationalisation activities carried out last year, as well as ongoing productivity improvements, would show positive results.</p>
<p>The company said that although indications were that it was entering a more satisfactory trading period, it preferred to wait for more definite signs of sustainable improvement in world textile demand before predicting a return to profitability.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
